   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: 1a. CMIASP-AF preparation documents completed and finalized in Nov 2013; ADB approved funding on 10 Apr 2014.

1b. At least 30% of CMIASP-AF subprojects prepared to PAC approval completed. Feasibility studies for 77 batch-1 subprojects approved prior to loan approval.

1c. FHMRMP completed in June 2016.

1d. Priority River Basin Flood Risk Management Project (Package 7) - Fact-finding mission held from 18 to 29 Nov 2019. Loan documents under finalization for ADB interdepartmental circulation.

1e. Package 7 - Final DD for bid documents submitted on 10 October 2019.

Project implementation consultants TOR prepared and approved by DWRI on 21 October 2019, EOI issued on 31 October 2019. Waiting for Submission 1. 16 numbers of EOIs were received. PMU has submitted the evaluated shortlist to the DWRI for approval.

1f. Mechanized Irrigation Innovation Project (Package 6) Feasibility study is completed. Land acquisition and indigenous people plan and framework submitted on 29 Dec 2019. Consultant contract ended. Loan documents will be prepared in 2020.

At least 30% of IMP subprojects prepared to PAC approval was not feasible as the IMP identified many projects.

2a. Completed. TOR of the sections approved in Jul 2014; environmental and social safeguard guidelines endorsed by MEWRI on 23 Jul 2015.

2b. Completed. Orientation of all DWRI social and environment section staffs completed in 2014; TOT Training on the guidelines completed in Dec 2015. To date, only one environmental specialist is in the ECC section. GESI section does not exist anymore. MEWRI is preparing the next organigram for DWRI and both sections will be reestablished.

2c. 27 training courses completed (403 staffs from DWRI and MEWRI; with 17.62% of women staff participation). Women staff in DWRI are less than 10%.

2d. Completed. GESI guidelines on project planning and implementation prepared and completed; approved by MEWRI on 23 Jul 2015; GESI training of DWRI staff through several short-term orientation sessions and workshops/seminars completed. To date, GESI section does not exist anymore in DWRI.

3. Final Irrigation Master Plan (IMP) submitted on 12 Sep 2019. IMP under finalization by DWRI for MEWRI final approval.

4a. Completed. FMU established on 13 Dec 2012; FMCB consultants with over 20% women mobilized from Apr 2013 until February 2019.

4b. Completed. Project M&amp;E systems developed in Mar 2014.

4c. Project completed on 31 Dec 2019. Closely monitoring submission of withdrawal applications for timely closure of project</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
